      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in Number 00-1595, Hoffman Plastic Compounds, Inc. v. The National Labor Relations Board. Mr. McCortney."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The issue in this case is whether the award of back pay to an undocumented alien who never was legally present or legally authorized to work in this country conflicts with this Court's holding in Sure-Tan or with this country's immigration laws and policies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The fatal flaw in the board's position lies in its adherence to its physical availability doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCORTNEY: Yes, Your Honor, the passage of IRCA in 1986."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus (States)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0000-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCORTNEY: Your Honor, I -- in the amicus brief of the States they seem to equate back pay under the NLRA with back pay under the FLSA when they're two different things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What about title VII?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCORTNEY: It would be -- if -- in your situation, you would get back pay, and let me explain the difference in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: If I could just supplement that, do we owe any deference to the views of the Attorney General of the United States, who is responsible for enforcing these -- both statutes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Immigration and Naturalization Service (INS)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WOLFSON: The INS has agreed with it and accepts it, and I'm here representing --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mitigation is quite impossible, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What it's doing, though, really is kind of odd, because the result is that back pay awards to illegal workers are likely to be greater than to legal ones under this board's policy, and that's so odd, and it gives the illegal alien an incentive to try to phony up more documents and to extend for the longest possible time the charade that the worker is here lawfully, and that's surely strongly against the policies of the immigration act at the very least."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wolfson",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1595",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "64adf5c7e0fbd6b4861ea45100bbec4795b9d9123a20d914c5e3407644789d0e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64adf5c7e0fb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WOLFSON: I think that the board is fashioning a rule that is implementing Congress' policy objective in IRCA across the board."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
